Merge release/v1.0.2 into devin/dr-s2: rollback-safety telemetry

The merge keeps the journal-shape telemetry (journal_snapshot_version_
max, journal_max_ws, workspace-scoped live count) and the three-number
--journal-format contract, and drops the v1.0.2 park: this branch's
registry is (ws, name)-keyed, so tenant runs dispatch in their own
workspaces — parking them here would disable the feature. The guard's
ws check now means "the target handles ws!=0 safely": this binary
does by executing, v1.0.2 does by parking, anything older refuses.

Tests flipped to workspace-aware semantics: tenant runs dispatch,
tenant attempts expire, snapshots keep scope, and the e2e proves a
replayed tenant run reaches only its own workspace's registration.

